<p>Mali&#x27;s military leader, Assimi Goita, made his first public appearance and delivered a televised address on Tuesday after coordinated weekend attacks by West Africa&#x27;s al-Qaeda affiliate JNIM and the Tuareg-dominated Azawad Liberation Front. The attacks struck sites including Mali&#x27;s main army base and the area near Bamako&#x27;s airport. Goita said the security situation was &quot;under control,&quot; acknowledged its &quot;extreme gravity&quot; and vowed to neutralise those responsible. The attacks killed Defence Minister Sadio Camara, according to News24, Dhaka Tribune, Africanews and SABC. A hospital source cited by AFP put the wider death toll at at least 23 civilians and soldiers. Insurgents also pushed Russian troops backing government forces out of Kidal in northern Mali, while the Azawad Liberation Front said it had taken the strategic town. Goita&#x27;s office said he met Russian Ambassador Igor Gromyko in Bamako and discussed the attacks and the partnership between Bamako and Moscow. Prime Minister Abdoulaye Maiga visited some of the wounded on Monday and urged the public not to give in to panic after the attacks.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/lcsEUXN1__nbhew9tmCQczzWzHpIP5AW7ZX5mvGFTUtVI0mr9dArdOQonUMZ5aCehjmmpAjX2t9dp_Xl8LmRC3qZ7BKvB7QLxDrZ7PcsYKd7nLfZRIMdUE3cH9oCGl_DiEqHpSP8wiR6x67m0eDTgGvyx_NvjPdph6fqNhrf__6VYmbYkykSEssrez6_6dhSfZP8CG0XMUQDmaEwrFgeBDCe20YfVrhY0DbhzIMdaWFzBwoNxosJdMjrN78mz5o-ishfk4WZkOU' alt='A Malian soldier takes position during an attack on Mali&#x27;s main military base at Kati, near Bamako, on April 25, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Bamako threat: JNIM announced the beginning of a &quot;total siege&quot; on Mali&#x27;s capital Bamako, and Swiss outlets reported that the group threatened a blockade on roads leading to the city.</li><li>Russian account: Nhan Dan reported that Russia&#x27;s defence ministry released video of fighting and said Africa Corps forces helped prevent a large-scale attack on Mali&#x27;s authorities.</li><li>Islamic State: SABC said Islamic State in the Sahel Province did not join Saturday&#x27;s attacks, but later reported Islamic State fighters entering an eastern town as Malian forces regrouped in the north.</li><li>Maghreb concerns: Courrier International reported that countries in the Maghreb feared for the security of their borders after the coordinated offensive in Mali.</li></ul><blockquote>(It) tells every Malian, every regional capital, and every foreign partner that JNIM can operate at will inside the supposedly secure heart of the state. - Justyna Gudzowska</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Malian military government: Goita called for a &quot;national surge&quot; and urged Malians to reject division, presenting the offensive as an attempt to fracture national unity. (<a href='https://www.letemps.ch/articles/apres-les-attaques-au-mali-le-chef-de-la-junte-affirme-que-la-situation-est-maitrisee'>Le Temps</a>)</li><li>Russia: The Malian presidency&#x27;s account cited by SABC said Gromyko reaffirmed Moscow&#x27;s commitment to support Mali in the fight against international terrorism. (<a href='https://www.sabcnews.com/sabcnews/mali-leader-meets-russian-envoy-as-attacks-escalate/'>SABC News</a>)</li><li>Mali&#x27;s prime minister: Abdoulaye Maiga urged national cohesion after the attacks. (<a href='https://africa24tv.com/mali-le-premier-ministre-abdoulaye-maiga-prone-la-cohesion-nationale'>Africa24 TV</a>)</li><li>Security analyst Corinne Dufka: Dufka said the weekend offensive had changed JNIM&#x27;s position in Mali, as the group and Tuareg separatists openly discussed cooperation. (<a href='https://www.sabcnews.com/sabcnews/mali-at-risk-of-splintering-after-jihadi-and-separatist-attacks/'>SABC News</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/video/newsfeed/2026/4/29/malis-military-leader-emerges-after-alleged-coup-attempt'>Mali’s military leader emerges after alleged coup attempt</a> 